# Mixed Miles Backend

Multi-tenant community events + membership + marketplace platform.
Clients: iOS, Android, Web app, plus Admin & City Founder web dashboards.

## Stack (do not deviate without being asked)
- Python 3.12, Django 5 + Django REST Framework (DRF)
- PostgreSQL (primary + read replica); no other relational DB
- Redis: cache, sessions, Celery broker, Channels layer, rate limiting
- Celery + Celery Beat for ALL async and scheduled work
- Django Channels for realtime chat
- S3 + CDN for media (presigned uploads only)
- Managed services: payment gateway (+webhooks), FCM/APNs, WhatsApp Business API, SES/SendGrid
- ASGI (Uvicorn/Gunicorn). App servers MUST stay stateless.

Never introduce FastAPI, Flask, SQLAlchemy, Mongo, or GraphQL unless explicitly asked.

## Golden rules
- Business logic lives in `services.py` (writes) / `selectors.py` (reads), not in views/serializers/models.
- Views stay thin. Cross-app access goes through the other app's service layer.
- When unsure about tenancy or a requirement conflict, ASK — don't guess.
- Do not write README.md
